<Layout title="Architectural Design Firm vs. Drafting Service | ATECT Architecture" description="Understand the difference between architectural design services and drafting-only services, including design, planning, construction documents and 3-D visualization.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Design & Documentation</div><h1>Architectural Design Firm vs. Drafting Service: What's the Difference?</h1><p>When planning an addition, renovation, custom home or commercial project, it is important to understand the difference between developing a design and simply producing drawings.</p></section>
<section class="section comparison-section"><div class="comparison-grid">
<article class="comparison-card"><div class="eyebrow">Drafting-Focused Services</div><h2>Drawing production</h2><p>A drafting service generally focuses on producing drawings from an established concept, sketch or direction. The exact scope varies by provider.</p><ul><li>Floor plans</li><li>Elevations</li><li>Basic sections</li><li>Existing-condition drawings</li><li>CAD documentation</li><li>Drawing revisions</li></ul></article>
<article class="comparison-card dark"><div class="eyebrow">ATECT Architecture</div><h2>Design + planning + documentation</h2><p>ATECT Architecture is an architectural design firm with architects and design professionals who can support projects from early planning through architectural documentation.</p><ul><li>Project planning</li><li>Architectural design</li><li>Space planning</li><li>Design development</li><li>Construction documents</li><li>3-D visualization</li></ul></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section alt"><div class="section-intro"><div class="eyebrow">The Key Difference</div><h2>Designing the project is different from documenting an established idea.</h2><p>If your design is already developed and you primarily need someone to produce drawings, drafting may be appropriate. If you need help determining what should be designed, how spaces should function, how an addition connects to an existing building, or how the project should be developed into coordinated documents, an architectural design firm may provide a broader scope.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-intro"><div class="eyebrow">What ATECT Provides</div><h2>From the first idea to the next phase.</h2></div><div class="service-grid">
<article><span>01</span><h3>Design</h3><p>Develop architectural concepts and solutions around the project's goals, property and intended use.</p></article>
<article><span>02</span><h3>Planning</h3><p>Consider existing conditions, project requirements, site considerations and potential design approaches.</p></article>
<article><span>03</span><h3>Documentation</h3><p>Develop architectural drawings and construction documents that communicate the proposed work.</p></article>
<article><span>04</span><h3>Visualization</h3><p>Use 3-D architectural renderings and related visual tools to help clients understand the proposed design.</p></article>
<article><span>05</span><h3>Coordination</h3><p>Support the organization and development of project information as the design moves toward the next phase.</p></article>
<article><span>06</span><h3>Project Support</h3><p>Provide architectural design and documentation support tailored to the scope of the individual project.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Explore ATECT</div><h2>See how our services connect.</h2><p>Explore construction documentation, residential architecture and the project process, then tell us what you are planning.</p></div><div class="link-grid"><a href="/architectural-construction-documents"><strong>Construction Documents</strong><span>Explore documentation →</span></a><a href="/residential-architecture"><strong>Residential Architecture</strong><span>Explore residential services →</span></a><a href="/process"><strong>Our Process</strong><span>See how we work →</span></a><a href="/contact" class="dark"><strong>Start a Project</strong><span>Tell us what you're planning →</span></a></div></section>
</Layout>
